+[Term]
+id: MONDO:7770736
+name: TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy
+def: "A Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the TSEN2 gene. It is characterized by intellectual disability, growth delay, hypotonia, motor delay, ataxia, visual impairment, and brain structural anomalies including pontine and cerebellar hypoplasia, cortical atrophy, and dilated ventricles, and may also present with proteinuria, thrombotic microangiopathy, severe hypertension, and end-stage kidney disease." [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/, PMID:34964109, PMID:38347586]
